<section class="hero shell">
  <div class="hero-copy">
    <span class="eyebrow"><i></i> Independent vulnerability research</span>
    <h1>Where software stops keeping its promise.</h1>
    <p class="hero-lede">I research browser, mobile, and web application trust boundaries. LLMs accelerate the search; reproducible evidence decides what is real.</p>
    <div class="hero-actions">
      <a class="button primary" href="<%= base('/research/') %>">Explore research</a>
      <a class="button" href="<%= base('/discoveries/') %>">View disclosures</a>
    </div>
    <div class="focus-row" aria-label="Research focus areas">
      <span>Browser security</span>
      <span>Android &amp; mobile</span>
      <span>Web AppSec</span>
      <span>LLM-assisted research</span>
    </div>
  </div>
  <aside class="research-console" aria-label="Public research archive summary">
    <div class="console-bar"><span><i></i><i></i><i></i></span><b>PUBLIC-RESEARCH-INDEX.json</b></div>
    <div class="console-body">
      <div class="console-stat"><strong><%= @discoveries.length %></strong><span>public CVEs</span></div>
      <div class="console-stat"><strong><%= @articles.length %></strong><span>archived articles</span></div>
      <div class="console-lines">
        <div><span>browser.engine</span><b>Edge / Firefox / Safari</b></div>
        <div><span>research.mode</span><b>human-led + LLM-accelerated</b></div>
        <div><span>validation.gate</span><b>reproduction + impact</b></div>
        <div><span>status</span><b class="status-live">PUBLIC</b></div>
      </div>
      <div class="signal-grid" aria-hidden="true"><span></span><span></span><span></span><span></span><span></span><span></span><span></span><span></span><span></span><span></span><span></span><span></span></div>
    </div>
  </aside>
</section>

<section class="metric-strip">
  <div class="shell metric-grid">
    <div><strong>05</strong><span>Public CVEs</span></div>
    <div><strong>03</strong><span>Browser engines</span></div>
    <div><strong>09</strong><span>Research articles</span></div>
    <div><strong>01</strong><span>Rule: proof over suspicion</span></div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section shell">
  <div class="section-heading">
    <div><span class="eyebrow">Selected research</span><h2>Work with the proof attached.</h2></div>
    <p>Root cause, attacker control, trust-boundary crossing, and demonstrated consequence—not a scanner dump.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="research-grid featured-grid">
    <% @featured_articles.each_with_index do |article, index| %>
      <%= article_card(article, index: index + 1) %>
    <% end %>
  </div>
  <a class="section-link" href="<%= base('/research/') %>">Browse the full research archive <span>↗</span></a>
</section>

<section class="section section-ruled">
  <div class="shell">
    <div class="section-heading compact-heading">
      <div><span class="eyebrow">Coordinated disclosure</span><h2>Public discoveries.</h2></div>
      <a class="button small" href="<%= base('/discoveries/') %>">All discoveries</a>
    </div>
    <div class="discovery-list">
      <% @discoveries.first(3).each_with_index do |discovery, index| %>
        <%= discovery_row(discovery, index: index + 1) %>
      <% end %>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section shell method-preview">
  <div class="section-heading">
    <div><span class="eyebrow">Research method</span><h2>LLMs widen the search. Controls keep it honest.</h2></div>
    <p>The method separates a plausible code path from a vulnerability that deserves a report.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="method-grid">
    <article><span>01</span><h3>Model the boundary</h3><p>Map actors, data, authority, expected guards, and the security promise under test.</p></article>
    <article><span>02</span><h3>Trace source to sink</h3><p>Use focused LLM-assisted review to connect attacker control to a sensitive operation.</p></article>
    <article><span>03</span><h3>Build the oracle</h3><p>Test the earliest unknown edge with exact artifacts, positive controls, and guarded negatives.</p></article>
    <article><span>04</span><h3>Prove the impact</h3><p>Promote only reproducible, attacker-observable consequences with honest limitations.</p></article>
  </div>
  <a class="section-link" href="<%= base('/method/') %>">Read the complete method <span>↗</span></a>
</section>

<section class="contact-band">
  <div class="shell contact-grid">
    <div><span class="eyebrow">Contact</span><h2>Have a difficult trust boundary worth investigating?</h2></div>
    <div><p>Available for authorized security research, source review, and research collaboration.</p><a class="button primary" href="mailto:jodyritonga@gmail.com">jodyritonga@gmail.com</a></div>
  </div>
</section>
